From 1c71591b764eba63d2646f899fc6c8005b722a7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: faycal <faycalelhandi9@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:26:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/35] feat(hybrid): lazy start, direct-memory exports and GPU
 event proxy (milestone 2b)

- Unbound exports now trap into a resolver that saves every System V
  argument register, loads the host module (libAstroHybridHost.prx), binds
  the table, starts the renderer and continues the call.
- The 13 direct-memory libkernel NIDs the game imports are exported (Kyty's
  kernel memory owns GPU-visible memory in the hybrid); AnyPS5 modules'
  extra imports (AgcAcbRewind, AgcDriverDeleteEqEvent) are added: 97 NIDs.
- ABI 1.1 adds donate_guest_range: the host releases a guest address window
  before Kyty's memory reserves free space.
- GPU events: registrations go to the host queue and to a Kyty proxy queue;
  a pump thread forwards Kyty's EOP and flip events to the host.

kytyGpuLoadTest: 410/411 checks; --lazy: first call starts Kyty (403 ms) and
returns the right result through the trap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
